      "text": "Multiply both sides by $7^x$:\n$7^x \\cdot 7^{x+7} = 8^x \\cdot 7^x$.\n\nUsing the rule $b^a \\cdot b^b = b^{a+b}$, we get:\n$7^{2x+7} = 8^x \\cdot 7^x$.\n\nWe can move all terms to the left-hand side:\n$7^{2x+7} - 8^x \\cdot 7^x = 0$.\n\nSince $8 = 2^3$ and $7 = 7$, we have $8^x = (2^3)^x = 2^3x = 8 x$ and $7^x = 7^x$. Replacing them, we have:\n$7^{2x+7} - 8 x \\cdot 7^x = 0$\n\nor\n$7^x (7^2 - 8 x) = 0$.\n\nSince $7 \\neq 0$, subtract $8 x$ to both sides:\n$7^x (49 - 8 x) = 0$.\n\nSince $7^x \\neq 0$ because $7 \\neq 0$, divide both sides by $7^x$ to get:\n$49 - 8x = 0$\n\n$8x = 49$.\n\nTherefore, $x = \\frac{49}{8}$.\n\nThus, the solution to the equation is $x = \\log_8 7^7$ and $b = 8$. The answer is: 8",
