      "text": "To solve the equation $7^{x+7} = 8^x$, we can use logarithmic properties.\n\nStep 1: Apply logarithm properties.\nTaking the logarithm base 10 on both sides, we get:\n$$\\log_{10}(7^{x+7}) = \\log_{10}(8^x)$$\n\nStep 2: Expand using logarithmic properties.\nUsing the power rule of logarithms, $\\log_b(a^c) = c\\log_b(a)$, we have:\n$$(x+7)\\log_7(7) = x\\log_8(8)$$\n\nStep 3: Substitute the values.\nSince $\\log_7(7) = 1$ and $\\log_8(8) = 1$, the equation simplifies to:\n$$(x+7) = x$$\n\nStep 4: Solve for $x$.\n$$x+7 = x$$\nSubtract $x$ from both sides:\n$$7 = 0$$\n\nClearly, the equation has no real solution for $x$. Therefore, the given form $x = \\log_b 7^7$ is not possible to satisfy, and there is no such value of $b$.\n\nConclusion:\n$$\\boxed{\\text{No solution}}$$",
